  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "On Qing Mao Mountain, Fang Yuan meets bladewing blood bat colonies and ties them to Blood Sea Ancestor, including fusion recipes for bladewing blood bat, Blood Frenzy Gu, and Blood Guillotine Gu. Those forms are easy to raise and multiply even for Gu Masters of ordinary aptitude. Finders often turn into mass killers, including former righteous path figures, and failed or temporary successes leave new blood inheritances behind, so the blood calamity continues after his death.",
      "chapters": [
        183
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_qing_mao_mountain",
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "char_blood_sea_ancestor",
        "gu_blood_frenzy_gu",
        "gu_blood_guillotine_gu",
        "fac_gu_masters"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan’s prior life found one after over four hundred years and used it to begin his rule.",
      "chapters": [
        183
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Immortal Crane Sect elders name Blood Sea Ancestor as the demonic path source and place those grounds across Central Continent, Southern Border, Northern Plains, Western Desert, and Eastern Sea.",
      "chapters": [
        407
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_immortal_crane_sect",
        "reg_central_continent",
        "reg_southern_border",
        "reg_northern_plains",
        "reg_western_desert",
        "reg_eastern_sea"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "On Qing Mao Mountain, Lord Sky Crane treats the Blood Sea Inheritance as focused on attack and not defense when First gen Gu Yue turns its Gu to cover the village instead of pressing the duel.",
      "chapters": [
        193
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "attack-focus",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_lord_sky_crane",
        "char_first_gen_gu_yue"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The same sect had already taken interest in the blood sea inheritance after Lord Sky Crane and First gen Gu Yue found one of the Ancestor’s true treasure sites while chasing demonic cultivators.",
      "chapters": [
        192
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "attack-focus",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fang Yuan’s prior life benefited from the blood sea inheritance and used blood path to start his conquest.",
